  "why_corrected": "This list was assembled by CRAWLING, not by being given names. 51 groups were tested, so an uncorrected table would show roughly one in twenty as unusual with nothing unusual happening. Benjamini-Hochberg at q controls the false discovery rate across the whole set: of the groups called significant here, about q of them are expected to be ordinary.",
